From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Liu <yangliu.leo@bytedance.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Sep 2024 16:57:50 +0800
Subject: feat: support application DLL blocklists in the early loading
 framework

Adapt the original dllBlocker implementation to Chromium 156. Store application
blocklists in the registry and initialize the existing NtMapViewOfSection hook
before Electron starts. Keep Chromium's startup safety beacon and buffer blocked
DLL notifications until the application registers its callback.

Use native registry access and a NUL-separated UTF-8 cross-module interface.
Preserve the original TTBlocklist REG_SZ JSON array using JsonCpp, so existing
application blocklists remain effective without a storage migration.
Electron initializes its own crash reporter and extension-point policy.

